      <Comment>The phosphatase is specific for sucrose-6-phosphate. The enzyme activity is Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; dependent, but at an unusually low Ka of 8-9 uM for Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;. The Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; dependency can be partially replaced by Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;. The enzyme activity is inhibited by Zn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;. Sucrose is a weak inhibitor with a Ki of 200-240 mM |CITS: [11050182]|.</Comment>
